h('Project Identity'); p('Project name: Sahayak\nProject category: Multilingual AI citizen assistance and service automation\nPrimary users: Citizens seeking accessible guidance and service support')
page('6 Project Write Up')
h('The Idea and the Problem')
p('We propose Sahayak as a single assistance workspace where citizens can ask questions, understand official information and receive guidance through service related tasks. A person may know the help they need but struggle to identify the correct portal, interpret a formal letter or work out which supporting documents to prepare. Language barriers and unfamiliar digital interfaces can make each of these steps harder. Sahayak brings conversation, document understanding and guided workflows into one interface so that users can move from a question to a practical next step.')
p('The project is intended for government services and can also support information and assistance across education, healthcare, banking, business and customer support. These are application areas for the platform, rather than claims of existing partnerships. The core use case is a citizen who needs an understandable explanation of a service and a clear path to act on that explanation.')
h('The Proposed User Experience')
p('A user selects a preferred language and enters a question by typing or speaking. The assistant retrieves relevant published material and prepares a response in the selected reply language. Where source material is available, the answer includes references that the user can inspect. The user can then open a relevant service, review requirements or request further explanation. Source references help make the response traceable, although their presence alone does not prove that every generated statement is correct.')
p('For a letter or notice, the user can upload an image or PDF and ask for a plain language explanation, action steps or deadlines. For a supported form, extracted information can be used to assist entry, with the user reviewing the details before continuing. The workspace also includes application records, documents, grievances, reminders and a route to request human support. Actual processing by an external authority depends on the relevant integration and approval process.')
h('Objectives')
p('The first objective is to reduce the effort required to understand service information through language choice, voice interaction and simple explanations. The second is to connect answers with actionable guidance, including required documents and supported form workflows. The third is to improve transparency through visible source references and opportunities to report unhelpful or outdated responses.')
p('A further objective is to support continuity: users should be able to return to their saved records and follow up on tasks. The project also aims to connect digital guidance with physical assistance through a sourced help centre directory. Success would mean that users can understand what to do next, identify the relevant source and complete supported steps with fewer avoidable errors. These are intended outcomes; measured impact results remain your answer.')
page('Innovation and Project Capabilities')
h('What Makes the Approach Distinctive')
p('Sahayak combines multilingual conversation with document explanation and service workflows. Its innovation is the connection between understanding information and taking the next step. A user can begin with an everyday question, ask for clarification in the same workspace and move into a relevant task without repeatedly translating formal instructions into their own words. Voice input and audio output provide additional interaction choices for people who find typing or reading difficult.')
p('The platform specification covers the 22 scheduled Indian languages and English. This is the intended language scope, rather than a claim of equally tested quality in every language. The implementation gives the selected reply language precedence over the detected input language, which supports cases where a citizen types in one language but wants the answer in another. Translation quality, terminology and speech performance must be assessed separately for each language before a broad rollout.')
h('Traceable Assistance and Human Review')
p('The question answering pipeline uses retrieval from published knowledge sources, numbered citations and source excerpts. Administrative tools support knowledge management and operational oversight. The design also includes feedback and a human support handover path. Together, these features provide a way to inspect and improve responses when a question is ambiguous, a source is outdated or an automated answer is insufficient.')
p('Document explanation and field extraction make the assistant useful beyond general conversation. Users can ask what a notice means and review extracted values while preparing a form. These outputs should remain subject to user confirmation, particularly for names, dates, amounts and deadlines. The proposed implementation keeps the citizen responsible for confirming the information submitted through a supported workflow.')
h('Connecting Citizens with Local Assistance')
p('The nearby help centre module provides a practical bridge to in person assistance. The project documentation records a Tamil Nadu directory covering 38 district choices and 33 sourced welfare office entries. Office cards link to their directory sources. This gives the prototype a concrete regional starting point while leaving room for additional verified service categories and locations.')
p('The current directory has important limits. Verified office coordinates, opening hours and a district boundary dataset are not available in the recorded implementation. Manual district selection is therefore the reliable path; automatic district detection, distance sorting and dependable open now results should not be presented as ready for the current dataset. New locations should be added only after source review and periodic rechecking.')
h('Current Prototype and Validation')
p('The repository contains a React and TypeScript interface, an Express backend, server side Gemini integration and PostgreSQL persistence. Implemented routes and screens cover conversation, voice, document explanation, form extraction, records and administration. The project also includes progressive web app configuration and offline conversation handling. Offline support is limited to available cached information and queued questions; generating a new AI answer still requires connectivity.')
p('Recorded checks include TypeScript checking, production builds and targeted regression tests. A successful live multilingual answer and saved history round trip remains unverified in the available QA notes because generation encountered model availability, timeout and high demand errors. Broad usability, accessibility and language accuracy evaluation are still needed before production claims can be made.')
page('Proposed Implementation and Relevant Details')
h('System Design and Processing Flow')
p('The proposed deployment retains the existing web architecture. The React interface handles language selection, conversation, uploads and task screens. An authenticated Express API coordinates requests, retrieves source material and calls the AI service on the server. PostgreSQL stores the application records needed for continuity. Keeping model calls on the backend allows service credentials and request controls to be managed centrally.')
p('For a typical question, the backend identifies the requested language, retrieves relevant knowledge passages and supplies those passages to the answer generation step. The response is returned with its source references and saved for later access where appropriate. If retrieval is insufficient or generation fails, the interface should explain the limitation and offer a retry or human assistance route. For uploads, the system extracts or interprets content and presents the result for review before it is used in a task.')
h('Implementation Roadmap')
p('Phase one is to stabilise a focused pilot using a small set of services and reviewed source documents. The team should verify the complete question to answer to history flow, confirm extraction quality on representative documents and test failure recovery. The initial pilot location, participating institution, service partners and delivery dates are your answer.')
p('Phase two is to evaluate the experience with intended users. Tests should cover language switching, speech recognition, readable explanations, source usefulness and form completion. Users should be able to correct transcriptions and extracted details. Accessibility checks should include keyboard navigation, screen reader behaviour and small mobile screens. Feedback should guide changes before expanding the catalogue.')
p('Phase three is controlled expansion. This includes onboarding verified content, rechecking local directory records, assessing each additional language and connecting external systems only when authorised interfaces and service agreements are available. Official application submission, live status synchronisation and document wallet connections must be validated individually before being described as operational. The budget, timeline and confirmed integration partners are your answer.')
h('Responsible Operation and Evaluation')
p('The rollout should minimise collection of personal information, explain why uploads are needed and obtain appropriate consent. Account access, permissions, upload handling, retention and deletion should be reviewed before public use. Generated guidance should preserve uncertainty and direct users to the relevant authority when a decision requires official confirmation. A service failure must not appear as a successful application or completed transaction.')
p('Evaluation should measure task completion, correction rates, answer usefulness, citation support, language quality and the time users need to understand the next step. Operational checks should track response latency, generation failures and the age of published sources. Targets and pilot results are your answer. These measures would test whether the platform improves access in practice and identify where human assistance remains necessary.')
h('7 Other Relevant Details')
p('Prototype status: Working codebase with implemented assistance modules and remaining live validation work.\nRepository or demonstration link: your answer\nTeam contact and mentor details: your answer\nHackathon participation date and venue: your answer\nAwards or recognition: your answer\nFunding requirement and deployment budget: your answer')
